    description: "FILED 2026-10-04 from WI-silos-mufon-mular-gavik-hihip-mibuj-mihov-julim (branch jgstern-agent/fix/silos).\n\nA closure CAPTURE LIST item with an initialiser, `{ [s = m] in s.x() }`, declares `s` inside the closure (type: m's). The binding pass records nothing for `capture_list_item`, so `s` falls through to the enclosing `s`. Live repro on origin/dev 385ec63be1 (and on the WI-silos branch, which does not touch capture lists):\n  func go(s: URLSession, m: FileManager) { run { [s = m] in s.zap3() } }\n  -> swift:URLSession:0-0:zap3:unresolved (should be FileManager, or at least not URLSession).\nFix shape: in the binding pass, a `capture_list_item` with `=` binds its simple_identifier into the lambda_literal's scope, typed by `_swift_receiver_expr_type` of the RHS (None when untyped, which still shadows). A bare `[weak self]` / `[unowned x]` item re-binds the same name to the same object and needs no entry.\nNot sized on the corpus."  # 286a
    fields: {}  # 286a
